<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Data-Structures on cesun.life</title><link>https://example.org/tags/data-structures/</link><description>Recent content in Data-Structures on cesun.life</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 16:39:49 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://example.org/tags/data-structures/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Linux Kernel Data Structures</title><link>https://example.org/linux-kernel-data-structures/</link><pubDate>Sat, 18 Feb 2023 08:20:51 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/linux-kernel-data-structures/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Linux&amp;rsquo;s list APIs are intrusive: linkage is embedded in the object owned by a subsystem. Intrusion removes a separate node allocation and lets one object participate in several indexes, but the container API does not own memory or provide synchronization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="circular-doubly-linked-lists"&gt;
 Circular Doubly Linked Lists
 &lt;a href="#circular-doubly-linked-lists" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;struct list_head&lt;/code&gt; contains only links:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-c" data-lang="c"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; list_head {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; list_head &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;next, &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;prev;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;};
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; job {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;unsigned&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;long&lt;/span&gt; id;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; list_head pending_link;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; list_head owner_link;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A list head has the same type as an embedded node. In an empty list, &lt;code&gt;next&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;prev&lt;/code&gt; both point back to the head. In a nonempty list, following either direction eventually returns to the head. Because the head is a sentinel rather than a payload object, iteration has no null terminator.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Misc Algorithms</title><link>https://example.org/misc-algorithms/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/misc-algorithms/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Use standard-library algorithms when their contract fits the task because their implementations optimize for the target platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="nearest-smaller-element-to-the-left"&gt;
 Nearest Smaller Element to the Left
 &lt;a href="#nearest-smaller-element-to-the-left" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Maintain increasing values on the stack. Each index is pushed and popped once, giving \(O(n)\) time and \(O(n)\) space.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;cpp&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cpp" data-lang="cpp"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#include&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;&amp;lt;cstddef&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#include&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;&amp;lt;vector&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;std&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;vector&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; nearest_left_smaller(&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; std&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;vector&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; values) {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; std&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;vector&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; result(values.size(), &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;);
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; std&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;vector&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;std&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;size_t&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; stack;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; stack.reserve(values.size());
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (std&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;size_t index &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;; index &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; values.size(); &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;++&lt;/span&gt;index) {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;stack.empty() &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; values[stack.back()] &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; values[index]) {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; stack.pop_back();
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;stack.empty()) {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; result[index] &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;static_cast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;(stack.back());
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; stack.push_back(index);
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; result;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/code&gt; when an equal predecessor is valid. Reversing the scan or comparison produces next-greater, stock-span, histogram, and temperature-query variants.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>